      "message": "Can you explain why this needs to be weak? If I understand correctly (but I\u0027m not sure I do), it might be something like this:\n\n    // This object is never garbage collected because the Tethering code running in\n    // the system server always maintains a reference to it for as long as\n    // mCallback is registered.\n    //\n    // Don\u0027t keep a strong reference to TetheringManager because otherwise\n    // TetheringManager cannot be garbage collected, and because TetheringManager\n    // stores the Context that it was created from, this will prevent the calling\n    // Activity from being garbage collected as well.\n\nIf the above is correct, then there is still a leak here: because mCallback is never unregistered, then the system server callback entry will never be freed, and no TetheringCallbackInternal objects will ever be freed. I think you might be able to fix that by adding a finalize method to TM, like so:\n\n    public void finalize() {\n        getConnector(c -\u003e c.unregisterTetheringEventCallback(mCallback,\n                mContext.getOpPackageName()));\n    }\n\n... but let\u0027s not do that in this CL.\n\nPer IM discussion: before we merge this CL, let\u0027s add check whether the comment suggested above is correct, and if so, add it. I think we can check by adding code to Tethering#doDump that prints all the elements of mTetheringEventCallbacks (assuming that can be done safely without locking problems) or at least prints the result of mTetheringEventCallbacks.getRegisteredCallbackCount().",
